[research] Read Time Series Momentum (Moskowitz, Ooi, Pedersen, 2012, JFE) (https://www.aqr.com/Insights/Research/Journal-Article/Time-Series-Momentum) — The sign of a security's own past 12-month (and shorter) return predicts its future return across 58 instruments; a volatility-scaled long/short built on this earns large, persistent abnormal returns, strongest at trend extremes.; Risks and Returns of Cryptocurrency (Liu & Tsyvinski, 2021, RFS) (https://academic.oup.com/rfs/article/34/6/2689/5912024) — Cryptocurrency returns are strongly predicted by their own momentum — past 1-to-4-week returns forecast future returns — with no exposure to traditional asset-class factors, consistent with investor underreaction.; The Original Turtle Trading Rules (Faith) (https://www.turtletrader.com/rules/) — Trade N-day (20/55) Donchian channel breakouts, size each position so 1 ATR of adverse move equals a fixed fraction of equity, and exit on an opposite shorter-channel break — a rules-based trend system whose edge is a few large winners paying for many small losers.; Chandelier Exit (Chuck LeBeau, via ChartSchool) (https://school.stockcharts.com/doku.php?id=technical_indicators:chandelier_exit) — A trailing stop set at the highest high since entry minus a multiple (≈3) of ATR keeps a position in a trend while volatility is normal and exits automatically when price falls a volatility-scaled distance from its peak.
[hypothesis] Crypto prices trend: a breakout above the prior 20-day high, taken only while price is above its 100-day EMA and sized so a 3-ATR stop risks 0.75% of equity, will capture enough of crypto's fat right-tailed moves to beat +5.05% in 2026; it is false if trailing-stopped exits leave average per-trade P&L below the 0.30% round-trip cost or if the triple exit still breaches the 25% drawdown mandate.
