[research] Read Bitcoin intraday time series momentum (Shen, Urquhart & Wang, Financial Review 2022) (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/fire.12290) — A constructive first part of the Bitcoin trading day predicts continuation into the last part; the effect is strongest on high-volume/high-volatility sessions, is driven by liquidity provision rather than late-informed trading, and yields the largest economic gains during market downturns — supporting a cycle-agnostic intraday hold whose winners are allowed to run to the close.; VWAP Intraday: Bounces, Reclaims and Failures (ChartMini) (https://chartmini.com/blog/vwap-trading-strategy-how-to-trade-with-institutional-flow-2026) — A VWAP 'reclaim' — price moving from below the session VWAP back above it and holding — is a watched intraday continuation setup because VWAP is the institutional execution benchmark that algos buy below and sell above, making it act as intraday support once reclaimed.; How Institutions Use VWAP: The Execution Benchmark Guide (ValorAlgo) (https://www.valoralgo.com/blog/vwap-trading-doctrine-institutional-guide) — VWAP is the benchmark institutional desks are measured against, so VWAP/TWAP execution algorithms mechanically accumulate below it and distribute above it, giving the level real order-flow support and making a confirmed reclaim a genuine shift of intraday control rather than a chart artifact.
[hypothesis] On a liquid crypto major, the first daily reclaim of the session anchored-VWAP (price crossing back above VWAP after trading below it, confirmed by an up-bar on above-average volume) marks intraday buyers regaining control and predicts positive continuation into the UTC close; it is false if the average return from a confirmed morning reclaim to the close does not clear the 0.30% round trip, in which case this returns at or below the incumbent.
