[hypothesis] A crypto major held while its price sits within 5% of its rolling 20-day high, and sold once it falls 15% below that high, earns more net of the 0.30% toll than the incumbent's fixed-hold time-series momentum, because George & Hwang's anchoring effect makes assets near a salient recent high underreact and keep drifting up; it is false if the near-high band captures no more of 2026's up-moves than 24 fixed-hold re-entries did, or if the 15% breakdown exit fails to keep the run inside the 25% drawdown mandate.
